Body:
Not sure if this a bug, but opencode should suggest to increase it if it happens to often, I suppose.

Here is a simple example for zai coding plan, just put it to opencode config home directory e.g. ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json (create a new file or append to existing one into provider settings).
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "zai-coding-plan":{
      "options": {
        "timeout": 3000000,
        "chunkTimeout": 3000000
      }
    }
  }
}
```

> I'm able to call GPT-5.4 with the setup below:
> 
> "gpt-5.4": {
>   "name": "gpt-5.4",
>   "limit": {
>     "context": 1000000,
>     "output": 128000
>   },
>   "options": {
>     "reasoningSummary": null
>   },
>   "extra_body": {
>     "drop_params": true
>   }
> },
> I'm using opencode with version `1.2.27`

no joy -- still get reasoningSummary unknown parameter.

tried with previous example as follows and get an issue with max_tokens param:
```
"gpt-5.4": {
          "name": "gapt-5.4",
          "limit": {
            "context": 262144,
            "output": 25000
          },
          "modalities": {
            "input": ["text"],
            "output": ["text"]
          },
          "options": {
            "model":"gpt-5.4",
          }
        },
```

